\ Baseline probe: the linter does not yet AOT-compile. Eight private
\ linter / lexer words reached through `run-lint` are rejected by the C
\ emitter because their bodies use row-variable stack shapes the AOT
\ compiler cannot model yet: literal-count `array-n` packs, stack
\ shuffles and `dip` reaching below a word's declared inputs into the
\ symbolic row, `#nth!` indexed mutation, and `call`s to quotations of
\ unknown effect (rule `check>>` / `match:` quotations and `#each` /
\ `#map` bodies).
\
\ This pins the per-word blocker inventory. The golden shrinks as those
\ codegen gaps close and individual words start compiling.
use "lint" ;
use "lint-rules" ;
{ } run-lint drop
